  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing due to filesystem permissions on the upload directory \u2014 not DB or disk-full.\n\nRoot cause:\n- App `incidentlab-app-1` runs as `1000:1000` (E5) with bind-mount `/srv/lab-data` -> `/data` `rw:true` (E5).\n- Host path `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `owner_uid 0, owner_gid 0, mode 0755` with `app_user_can_write:false` for `1000:1000` (E7).\n- Parent `/srv/lab-data` is `owner 1000:1000, mode 0755` with `app_user_can_write:true` (E8), so only the `uploads` sub-directory is unwritable.\n\nSymptoms caused by it:\n- `POST /upload` fails in `os.replace(tmp_path, final_path)` with `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/tmp/...part' -> '/data/uploads/...'` (E4).\n- `/health` returns `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2) because health probe `open(probe,\"wb\")` fails with `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/uploads/.health-...'` (E4).\n- Both failures are writes to `/data/uploads`, same directory flagged unwritable in (E7).\n\nRuled out:\n- DB dependency healthy: `incidentlab-db-1` `state running, status Up 18 minutes (healthy)` (E1), `health: healthy, restart_count 0, running true` (E10), logs show normal `ready to accept connections` + routine checkpoints with no errors (E9).\n- Disk/inode exhaustion: `/srv/lab-data` `use_percent 3.6, inode_use_percent 0.1, available_mb 435.2` (E6).\n- Crash/restart loop: both containers `running` (E1), `restart_count 0` for app (E5) and db (E10), recent events show only `pg_isready` healthcheck `exec_die exit 0`, no `die/stop` for app (E3).\n\nFix requires approval (not applied): `chown 1000:1000 /srv/lab-data/uploads` and/or restore mode allowing app write, then verify `POST /upload` and `GET /health` return 200.\n",
